2131..2205 Comment "/// Reading twice is reading once at the same state. The inner `get` is an"
2206..2276 Comment "/// instance of the rule\'s own left side through its pattern, and both"
2277..2340 Comment "/// reducts read once and continue at that state three times. A"
2341..2492 Comment "/// scope over this theory runs its subject normalised by the rule: `let a = /// st.get(); let b = st.get(); pure a + b` reads once, `let a = st.get();"
2493..2566 Comment "/// pure a + a` with `b` bound to `a` (`state-laws.gandr`\'s `readTwice`)."
